Iteration Loop
1. Assume an initial descent velocity
2. Use the iterative procedure to get αF , forces, etc. as
described earlier
3. Compute required power: Main rotor power + Tail rotor power + Transmission losses
4. Compute available power = W * Descent velocity
5. Equate available power and required power by adjusting the descent velocity
6. Iterate step 2 to 5 until power needed = power available.
